    "updated_at": "2026-10-31T07:20:05Z",
    "body": "Resolved by Zooko's decision to document it, which is in 0.8: `submit_with`'s doc says a room's bytes on entry are unspecified, reused across streams, and that a program keeping one caller's secrets from another writes all of `room` and reads none of it first (`src/stream.rs` at the tag). With #204's fix, `fill` is told how much it must write, too. Ready to close, I think.\n\n\u2014 Devon Jonte\n",
